{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:31:40.408460Z","id":"83a2543bcb5633dd4b9f1b963e4fdee6e72091fde7a697b1d3aaf8eb3b6b1d55","body":{"detail":"Measured 2026-10-13 on one idle Mac (AC power), CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 npm run perf, main (579bdc8b) and rust-int (5fccef6b) alternating: main comment ready 99-100 ms in run 1 (failed, limit 86 at scale 1.00) and 91 ms in run 2 (passed, limit 94 at scale 1.09); rust-int 101-104 ms in four runs at scale 1.00-1.09 (failed) and 104-128 ms at scale 1.36-1.45 (failed on 128 vs 117). Cold ready latency is also at or over its 38 ms limit on both (39-41 ms). Logs: target/int/ttu-main-*.log and ttu-br-*.log in that worktree. Either the budget no longer matches this machine, or comment readiness regressed before main's tip; the branch adds roughly 3-10 ms on top.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"bdb9b4773ddf4cd164ffbfbeb2717bcfe8744d1cf5cd00d81b4975c37703047c"},"summary":"Time to usable's comment ready runs over its 86 ms darwin budget on main and on rust-int alike, the branch a few ms slower","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815194Z","id":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","body":{"detail":"The panel embeds the shell's Sidebar, ThreadCard and SendButton; the owner chip, the withheld label and the Send menu's grouping brought it to 65396 gzip bytes (from 65043), with the menu and the approval card moved into lazy chunks. The extension's own Send menu names (plan Task 23) have almost no room.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"935c259722638f24eea9dd631ad2e5f8cc1da6109229199e3b748da29265c76f"},"summary":"The extension panel is 140 bytes under its 65536 ceiling","tags":["task:23","bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.164076Z","id":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Confirmed with both builds' scripts/bundle-size.mjs: extension panel 65043 gzip bytes at a2378555, 65396 at f7a89d53 (ceiling 65536); questions 15125 -> 15564, people 12525 -> 12587; artifact unchanged at 64069, which equals its budget. The panel embeds the shell's SendButton and its lazy SendMenu, so names and person groups reach the extension's Send menu once its agents carry name and person; the panel's link from an approval item to the shell's inbox (spec 2026-10-08 section 17) is the next code to land there. Recommendation: decide the panel ceiling before that work (for example 66560, with a note of what grew) rather than squeezing; the 140 bytes left will not hold a link component and its styles.","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.260982Z","id":"2c03296e1e23090fbcdd86127cab3e21dd0ce1138e46921239907b0abf128436","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","summary":"After the round-1 fixes (bb547990) the extension panel measures 65526 of 65536 gzip bytes (10 left); the artifact entry measures 64062 of 64069, its Send default moved into the sidebar chunk.","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:40:37.891674Z","id":"ca2f1e9d1f8982634c233f3f36d8c5f2b825007457a5794e18be6e2eee744a14","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3ae32de","summary":"The owner raised extPanel to 66560 (874f36ab). With the panel's Send rule, the worker's approves-first lookup and the approval rows' link (a3ae32de), node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures: panel 66388 of 66560, artifact 64062 of 64069 and gallery 27929 of 27960 (both unchanged from 086b92c8), questions 15608 of 16384.","supersedes":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.546920Z","id":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §23: the people module is lazy (16 KiB), gallery and artifact grow by at most 512 bytes, extPanel stays within 65,536. Measured at 09672011 (node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs): panel 66,555 against 66,560 (raised in 874f36ab), artifact 64,062 against 64,069 (63,988 at the branch's base: 74 bytes over main, within the 512), people 13,636 against 16,384, gallery 27,929 against 27,960. Either the panel sheds about 1 KiB (for one, its Send menu and approval items loaded when first opened) or the spec's 65,536 is amended; the artifact entry needs room before its next change, up to main's size plus 512 once the branch is rebased and main's sizes measured again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bba27ecb5f1319da2af32bd259747e5f7245ba1bf7c1bc3fdbd2e87c31338ae2"},"summary":"extPanel's budget, 66,560 gzip bytes, is over spec §23's 65,536; the artifact entry has 7 bytes left","tags":["bundle","spec:23","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"5b1cd879b46b3c28d1a42687510efc263d42d6b73dc76166d32ea830e93e6302","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 66d2a8f3: gallery 27915, artifact 64069 (exactly at budget). With hosted mode: gallery 28063 (the dynamic import of web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte in web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts), artifact 64174 (NO_VIEWER in web/shell/src/threads.ts and the guest_name_required check in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts submitDraft). `--record` never raises a budget, so the raise is the owner's call. A separate signin.html entry was tried and cost more (the Svelte runtime split into two shared chunks, gallery 28698).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"22ba18f2fd9882bbc078f52c81a769741d83a1cbdbc951fea67e25b0a47d4354"},"suggested_fix":"Accept the raise, or move the sign-in pages out of the shell's bundles (server-rendered pages).","summary":"The gallery and artifact budgets were raised by hand for hosted mode (gallery 27960 to 28100, artifact 64069 to 64200)","supersedes":"f5acac29fd4ca2f1e5555e638561e97d1324b74586057a6115073d0311fc258b","tags":["status:needs-decision","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268606Z","id":"69f7b606f4cc4bce3e4bfc15e8dd6765243f8927caa408a5ed150549be6f11f8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5b1cd879b46b3c28d1a42687510efc263d42d6b73dc76166d32ea830e93e6302","summary":"Changed since recorded: the budgets are now gallery 27960 and artifact 64243 (web/perf/bundle-budget.json:3-4). The artifact entry's was set to the live layers' measured size by 4f68518e; the gallery's is back at its pre-hosted value. The raise this record asks the owner about is no longer in the file.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268733Z","id":"65344511aead0fc9df407cca5e428726e67dc64ebffaac6528f9d049ef8a2f65","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Changed since recorded: the extension panel's ceiling is 66560 gzip bytes (web/perf/bundle-budget.json:15), raised by 874f36ab at the owner's call. Proposed close: reason:obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:56:02.498969Z","id":"e2e655a2345a08b11a5996da4e81585b4f953862a0ceb9a3651725f1b63b3fde","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs (//web:bundle_size): extPanel 67,922 before, 66,027 after. web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte now imports Merge.svelte (the folded Merge pages section at the panel's foot) when it renders, as it already does InboxTab.svelte and Roster.svelte; the extension loads the chunk from its own files, so no network round trip is added. Moving web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts's notification text and URL filter out of the question module took about 125 more bytes off the panel. Reaching 65,536 would need another lazy part of about 500 bytes, for one Elsewhere.svelte (shown only when the site has threads on other pages) or SendButton's menu; the choice between that and amending the spec's 65,536 is still open.","kind":"comment","references":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","summary":"The panel measures 66,027 against its 66,560 budget, the budget unchanged; spec section 23's 65,536 is still 491 bytes away","tags":["bundle","spec:23","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:46:26.995763Z","id":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","body":{"detail":"Before the thread and in-terminal question surfaces (parent of commit 3f7e040cd) it measured 16073: index 2901, open 10878, inbox-model 2294 (gzip -9 of the files web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs counts). With them it is 16746: the sidebar's thread check and on-demand hook in the index chunk, the in_terminal branch and the on-demand import (with its preload list) in the open chunk QuestionList.svelte shares, and inThread/closedLabel in model.ts. Everything else already loads on demand from web/shell/src/q/where.ts (TerminalCard, ThreadLinks, thread-slots), which the script does not count; loading everything eagerly measured 17691, and also put the extension panel over its budget (67251 > 66560; now 66394). The script calls this ceiling the spec's and never records it, so a raise belongs to the owner. Options: raise questions to 16896 or 17408, or ask for further cuts (for example moving byThread out of QuestionFeed, or moving the shared .qcard frame CSS), which save tens of bytes, not hundreds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"edb8d25db9f80b9d4161f4375b98308d53ab2e317f39f3a593ad6a41286ad4d0"},"summary":"The question module measures 16746 gzip bytes against its 16384 ceiling, so //web:bundle_size fails","tags":["status:needs-decision","bundle","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:21:19.079589Z","id":"a800b624ee2291d23bb532c652d19d3ece9e0469836b45ce79c6cdcf4d062aa2","body":{"detail":"just web-test, //web:bundle_size: 'gzip bytes: ... questions 16828 ... panel 59195' and 'questions: 16828 gzip bytes, over its budget of 16384'. The 82 bytes beyond 16746 come from the thread link in the always-loaded QuestionCard (aboutLink in web/shell/src/q/model.ts) and QuestionList's thread prop. QuestionFeed.byThread moved into the on-demand ThreadQuestions. The panel fell from 66394 because its Page-view question block (web/extension/src/panel/PageQuestions.svelte) now loads on demand. The ceiling is unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","summary":"At 0b7e4d15e the question module measures 16828 gzip bytes (444 over 16384) and the extension panel 59195 (budget 66560)","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:01:13.074354Z","id":"bfc5fe5c7879bad0814800ce2948d258bf09dc219678753f4f0cecd43b185916","body":{"detail":"The gallery's unread summary (GallerySummary.svelte, with InboxRow.svelte, inbox-model.ts and open.ts, which only it and InboxPage use) left the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts no longer exports it). web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts summary() imports it as its own chunk, and Gallery.svelte loadQ starts it on / in the same Promise.all as q() and the inbox page, so no request waits on another. The artifact view never showed it. bazel test //web:bundle_size: questions 13444, gallery 27834 (budget 27960, 27798 before), artifact 63627 (63612 before), extension panel 59306 (unchanged). bazel test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=ask-where.spec: 24 passed, including the summary's terminal card and inbox row on /.","kind":"comment","references":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","summary":"At 00d63fea2 the question module measures 13444 gzip bytes (16887 at d8bb21429), the budget unchanged at 16384","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:01:13.074810Z","id":"b7cd30c21119e143c6b94bfaf973c7fc363b3af6189ba51def39ca26bf0a5b8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:00d63fea2","summary":"bazel test //web:bundle_size passes at 00d63fea2: questions 13444 gzip bytes against 16384","supersedes":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.470803Z","id":"717d283bc0cb09f010acc169dec8ca86f8466224ce7586bb137150fc48f808b7","body":{"detail":"Main measured exactly 28159 gzip bytes against a budget of 28159, so any gallery change needs room. The card's by-line gained `p.a.brief?.by ||` (web/shell/src/ui/GalleryCard.svelte), 13 gzip bytes after trying shorter forms. The alternatives are a chip from the lazy gallery module (cardMarkers), which would still read 'command line' in the by-line, or finding 13 bytes elsewhere in the gallery entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":3},"content_hash":"65bc77da077a9dd2aba522a02928bbbf96de8af6ffa3ef626701cfb384443519"},"summary":"The gallery's bundle budget was raised 13 bytes (28159 to 28172) for the gallery card naming who started an artifact from a brief","tags":["status:needs-decision","bundle","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:06:41.266877Z","id":"28f0e3b73a4e9701d32f13e35b03b0f710869021241aa2f18aae816a3c5117a6","body":{"detail":"The thread drawer (web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte, DrawerChrome.svelte, web/shell/artifact.html's clax-drawer script) brought the artifact entry from 63,997 to 64,241 gzip bytes, measured by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs under bazelisk test //web:bundle_size. Everything else about the drawer was moved into the sidebar's lazy chunk to fit; the next eager addition to the artifact entry will fail the gate unless the budget is raised or something eager is made lazy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"32dc2973c8ce2aff5dab4f49139a0b61663391620f3ba7116a4c5d265bb5703e"},"summary":"The artifact entry has 2 gzip bytes left under its budget (64,241 of 64,243) after the thread drawer's layouts","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
